#edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186370880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198421 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198421 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186435476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198421 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Non-Uniform, Non-Rectangular Laminar" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198421 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198421 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "aa0241de-b852-5c1f-962b-559e05edf39e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating the Radius of Gyration of a Plane Lamina" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050741 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1050 1380.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198500 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ee989efc-2e02-5faf-9663-d0e67a72db66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280894 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163011" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e1eb104-83e6-5dc7-913b-3996107f92c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198651 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the origin is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 2=4.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{0} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{8}{3}+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{3}+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{[\\frac{4}{3}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(4+9-(\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(13-\\frac{5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot \\frac{34}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{0}^{2}=\\frac{17}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186281256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1069 "q-163612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,4\\le y\\le 6\\}.$ Find the radius of gyration of the plate about the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2496e287-b250-5877-a40c-af954399de62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198665 #edb/ref 1074 "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{x}$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n${R}_{x}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{x}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{x}$ is the moment of inertia about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n${R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration ${R}_{0}$ about the origin is given by\n${R}_{0}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{0}}{M}},$\nwhere ${I}_{0}$ is the moment of inertia about the origin.\n\nThe moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is defined as\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function.\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\frac{1}{3}(1-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{4}^{6}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}[y]_{4}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(6-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}\\,⇒\\,{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199262 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199262 #edb/ref 1061 31767 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199262 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "76c2c5a5-4cc8-5b16-af7c-3ebae501b962" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199262 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199458 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199344 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199351 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199344 #edb/ref 1061 44959 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199344 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b8d3d2ed-b979-53cc-a718-ce66bcb92672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199344 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199348 #edb/ref 1061 45033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199348 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4f7fed02-59a7-5116-a7d3-2d07448fbbfa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199348 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199351 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199351 #edb/ref 1061 45077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199351 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b3e8808b-6d9a-533e-98f7-fae6b2f81961" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199351 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199368 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199368 #edb/ref 1061 45253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199368 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b488dfc8-1a77-5eca-8218-1163bb51565d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199368 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199458 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we discuss a concept analogous to *center of mass* that applies to rotating bodies.\n\nRecall that the *center of mass* of a plane lamina is defined as the point $(\\bar{x},\\bar{y})$ in the coordinate plane where the entire mass of the lamina could be concentrated to produce the same *total moment* about the coordinate axes as the original laminar. \n\nAnalogously, the **radius of gyration** of a plane lamina is the distance $R$ from an axis of rotation $L$ that the entire mass $M$ of the lamina would need to be concentrated to produce the same *moment of inertia* as the original lamina. \n\n![](images/c9/c9999bf30a93a857db731488739f0a640edc7b91de907cd772b777489a011fb8.png)\n\nTo derive an explicit formula for the radius of gyration, recall that the moment of inertia of a particle $P$ of mass $m$ at a distance of $r$ from an axis of rotation equals\n\n$$\nmr^2.\n$$\n\nSo, for a particle of mass $M$ at a distance of $R$ from the axis of rotation $L,$ the moment of inertia about $L$ is given by\n\n$$\nMR^2.\n$$\n\nThe radius of gyration is defined as the distance $R$ that a particle of mass $M$ must be placed to give the same moment of inertia as the original lamina. Therefore, it is the solution to the equation\n\n$$\nI = MR^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $I$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about $L.$\n\nRearranging this equation, we find that the radius of gyration is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I}{M}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199458 #edb/ref 1065 5074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199458 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9694de04-ca38-5d55-a60f-6663ca34e7cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199458 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199498 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll limit the axis of rotation to the $x$-axis, the $y$-axis, and the origin. We summarize the key results below:\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_x$ of a lamina about the $x$-axis is given by $R_x = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_x}{M}},$ where $I_x$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_y$ of a lamina about the $y$-axis is given by $R_y = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_y}{M}},$ where $I_y$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\n- The radius of gyration $R_0$ of a lamina about the origin is given by $R_0 = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{I_0}{M}},$ where $I_0$ is the moment of inertia of the lamina about the origin." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199498 #edb/ref 1065 7823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199498 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "096487a4-3e7b-571a-94b9-ec4e84d689bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199498 #edb/ref 1067 "A Summary of Key Results" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278599 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278599 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278599 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01f9db5c-e164-5da8-8198-fa6bb66ab5d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278612 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{9}{20}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278612 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278612 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "03680dad-3bcf-5b29-abba-9ff2a1e3d2a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278654 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{\\frac{17}{3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278654 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278654 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "06aa15d2-30ee-5cc9-b5dd-ac324e05cd6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278693 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278693 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278693 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a8c3f43-d62e-5000-aa73-65488d3b0b24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278716 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{3}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0d652bb7-2c2a-59df-a30e-8a26cac188ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278758 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{5}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "124a91eb-fdf5-5e37-9d33-f96d11c8d50d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186278827 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{5}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [